 colspan="1">miR-1010</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">dme-miR-1010</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">dme-miR-1016</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">miR-iab4as-3p</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">dme-miR-iab4as-3p</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">dme-miR-iab-4-3p</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">miR-iab4as-5p</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">dme-miR-iab4as-5p</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">dme-miR-iab-4-5p</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">dme-miR-iab-4-5p</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="nt102"><p>70/152 <italic>Drosophila</italic> miRNAs can be arranged into 24 groups that have sequence homology at the 5&#x02032; end (61 miRNAs, listed separately in <xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="pone.0002818.s008">Dataset S4</xref>) and/or over their entire length (38 miRNAs, listed separately in <xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="pone.0002818.s009">Dataset S5</xref>). See <xref ref-type="sec" rid="s4">Methods</xref> and text for explanation of match criteria. The miRNA group ID was chosen as the miRNA closest to the consensus sequence of the grouped related miRNAs. <italic>D. melanogaster</italic> miRNAs with 60&#x02013;69.9&#x00025; similarity over their full sequence are listed in <xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="pone.0002818.s010">Dataset S6</xref>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="pone-0002818-t003" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0002818.t003</object-id><label>Table 3</label><caption><ti