c>Drosophila</italic> miRNAs (<xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="pone.0002818.s012">Dataset S8</xref>). Group IDs correspond to <italic>C. elegans</italic> miRNAs with sequence-related miRNAs in <italic>Drosophila</italic>. Nematode-fly miRNAs with weaker identity (60&#x02013;69.9&#x00025;) over full sequence are listed in <xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="pone.0002818.s013">Dataset S9</xref>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="pone-0002818-t004" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0002818.t004</object-id><label>Table 4</label><caption><title>Analysis of 5&#x02032; and &#x02265;70&#x00025; full sequences identifies 76 <italic>C. elegans</italic>-human miRNA families including 76 worm miRNAs and 102 human miRNAs.</title></caption><graphic id="pone-0002818-t004-4" xlink:href="pone.0002818.t004"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" alternate-form-of="pone-0002818-t004-4"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">miRNA Group ID</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>C. elegans</italic> miRNA</td><td colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">Human related miRNAs</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5&#x02032; Sequence</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Full Sequence</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">let-7</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">cel-let-7</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hsa-let-7a</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hsa-let-7a</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hsa-let-7b</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hsa-let-7b</td></tr><tr><td align